<title>GREECE: GREEK SHIPOWNER LIVANOS DIES AFTER LONG ILLNESS.</title>
<headline>GREEK SHIPOWNER LIVANOS DIES AFTER LONG ILLNESS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek shipowner George Livanos died in Evangelismos hospital on Sunday following a long illness.</p>
<p>Livanos, 71, owned the largest fleet of Greek-registered ships with the largest tonnage. He also founded and owned the Ceres flying dolphin company, which links mainland Greece with the islands.</p>
<p>He had also founded the Hellenic Marine Environment Protection Agency (Helmepa), to increase awareness on issues of marine pollution among seamen and the public.</p>
<p>Livanos will be buried from the Athens Cathedral at 1030 GMT today.</p>
<p>-- Artemis Hionides, Athens newsroom 0031-1-3311813-4</p>
